    {
      "language": "en",
      "pointer": "/prose/6/text",
      "before": "Magnetic flux can be interpreted as the number of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$.\n\nSuppose that the number of magnetic field lines crossing a unit area perpendicular to the vector $\\vec{B}$ is defined to equal the vector's magnitude $B$.\n\nUnder this convention, the magnetic flux equals the number of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$.",
      "requiredAfter": "Magnetic flux can be interpreted as a directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$, with signs defined relative to the chosen normal to the plane of the loop.\nSuppose that the number of magnetic field lines crossing a unit area perpendicular to the vector $\\vec{B}$ is defined to equal the vector's magnitude $B$, with crossings along the chosen normal counted positively and crossings against it counted negatively.\nUnder this convention, magnetic flux equals the directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$.\nReversing the chosen normal reverses the sign of the flux. In the uniform-field, plane-loop case considered here, a geometrical count that ignores crossing direction corresponds only to the magnitude of the flux and does not change when the chosen normal is reversed.",
      "currentNativeText": "Magnetic flux can be interpreted as a directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$, with signs defined relative to the chosen normal to the plane of the loop.\n\nSuppose that the number of magnetic field lines crossing a unit area perpendicular to the vector $\\vec{B}$ is defined to equal the vector's magnitude $B$, with crossings along the chosen normal counted positively and crossings against it counted negatively.\n\nUnder this convention, magnetic flux equals the directed count of magnetic field lines passing through the area $S$.\n\nReversing the chosen normal reverses the sign of the flux. In the uniform-field, plane-loop case considered here, a geometrical count that ignores crossing direction corresponds only to the magnitude of the flux and does not change when the chosen normal is reversed.",
      "beforeSha256": "e60690d886e621296d23948a2e817031c77b6d9de2b2de55db31d0f7aef3316b",
